{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.BorromeanQuark","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.canonical","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L129-L143","doc":"**Faithful instance.**  Defines `bare_mass` literally as the\ntopological-volume formula `borromean_volume / (1 - 1/q)²`, so\n`volume_calibrates_mass` closes by `rfl`.\n\nThe `is_baryon_realisation` predicate is now the **canonical\nexistence statement**: the proton and neutron partitions both\ninhabit `BorromeanBaryon` and have the expected charge sums.\nDischarged by exhibiting `proton_partition` and `neutron_partition`\nas the canonical witnesses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass_from_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass_from_volume","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L120-L127","doc":"**Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond).**\nConditional on `[BorromeanQuark]`, baryon mass at every q > 1\nequals `borromean_volume / (1 − 1/q)²`. Fully verified by Lean\nonce an instance is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.is_baryon_realisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.is_baryon_realisation","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Every observed baryon is realised as a Borromean partition: the\nproton and the neutron both inhabit `BorromeanBaryon`, with the\ncolour triple `(0,1,2)` and their respective orientations.\n\n**Encoded 2026-09-13.**  This was two fields —\n`is_baryon_realisation : Prop` plus a witness of it — the first\ntyped with the *universe* `Prop`, so the instance chose the\nproposition and `⟨True, trivial⟩` would have discharged the pair.\n`baryon_mass_from_volume` and the `[BorromeanQuark]`-conditional\nresults downstream were therefore conditional on nothing from this\nfield.\n\n**The proposition below is the author's, not mine.**  It is exactly\nwhat `instance canonical` already supplied for the old `Prop` field,\nmoved from the instance into the class where it constrains every\ninstance rather than one.  Nothing is weakened and nothing is\ndecided: the canonical instance still discharges it, with the same\nterm (`⟨proton_partition, neutron_partition, rfl, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩`),\nso the carrier remains inhabited by real mathematics — which is what\nmakes the projection above a legitimate accessor rather than a\nself-assuming one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.volume_calibrates_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.volume_calibrates_mass","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L92-L92","doc":"The mass functional evaluates to `borromean_volume / (1 − 1/q)²`\nat every q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.bare_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.bare_mass","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The baryon mass functional (depends on q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L68-L118","doc":"**Conjecture class.** An instance asserts that the Borromean\nlink `B_3` is the canonical baryon model: nucleons (proton,\nneutron) are realised as Borromean-linked three-quark\nconfigurations with hyperbolic volume `borromean_volume ≈\n7.32772` (the topological mass scale).\n\nTwo conjectural fields:\n* `is_baryon_realisation` — every observed baryon arises as a\n  Borromean configuration with appropriate orientation/color;\n* `volume_calibrates_mass` — the bare baryon mass is\n  `borromean_volume / (1 − 1/q)²`, calibrating the\n  topological-mass formula at q = q₀.\n\n`sorry` in any concrete instance is understood as **conjecture**,\nnot missing proof. Downstream blocks may take `[BorromeanQuark]`\nas an explicit hypothesis to remain `theorem`/`proposition` per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Ch. 6 §3, conj:borromean-quark ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L61-L64","doc":"The baryon mass from the topological mass formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromean_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromean_volume","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.neutron_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.neutron_partition","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L48-L55","doc":"The neutron: one up (+1) and two down (-1), net charge 0.\nColor assignment: one quark per color tube (bijective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.proton_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.proton_partition","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L39-L46","doc":"The proton: two up (+1) and one down (-1), net charge +1.\nColor assignment: one quark per color tube (bijective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.charge_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.charge_sum","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The orientations sum to the net Coulomb charge ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.orientation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.orientation","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Crossing orientation: +1 (up) or -1 (down) for each component ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.color","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.color","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The three color tube assignments ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon","kind":"structure","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-quark.lean#L30-L37","doc":"The Borromean link of three unknots in color tubes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}